2.1 Job Purpose

Define and own the strategic direction for an Agentic AI–native infrastructure platform — where Infrastructure-as-Code, continuous compliance, and optimization are all delivered and governed by autonomous AI agents — in a self-motivated manner consistent with the TI strategy and Engineering Map.
Own strategy, architecture, and outcomes across >50% of infrastructure technology domains; serve as principal owner and key thought leader for codified, self-governing, and intelligent platform engineering.
Accountable for demonstrating the values of the organization (customer centricity, productivity, agility) by setting an example for others with respect to energy, motivation, quality of outcomes, and engagement; provide coaching and mentorship across TI and T&O.
Accountable for setting an example to mentor across TI by demonstrating organizational values and helping individuals achieve exemplary performance.

2.2 Primary Responsibilities
Supervise Team

Own quality, quantity, and timeliness of platform and capability delivery across IaC, compliance, and optimization — all underpinned by agentic AI.
Provide point of escalation and resolution for platform, service, and cross-domain issues.
Guide, coach, and mentor teams to drive optimal performance and develop next-generation cloud and agentic AI talent.
Own budget, FTE planning, performance management, and reporting for the sub-organization.

Contribute to and lead teams that:
Innovation

Establish Agentic AI as the foundational operating model across the infrastructure estate — MCP-based multi-agent systems applied to provisioning, governance, remediation, and lifecycle management, extending proven patterns (DR Advisor, OlympusAI).
Drive enterprise solution architectures for IaC at scale, policy-as-code, and self-service governance, with autonomous agents embedded across the delivery lifecycle.

Improvement

Accountable for the strategic technical direction of an agent-driven platform spanning IaC, continuous compliance, and optimization.
Embed agentic AI into compliance and governance — real-time control monitoring, configuration drift detection, and closed-loop autonomous remediation tied to ITSM and change governance — making the estate continuously audit-ready.
Apply agentic AI to continuously optimize cost, performance, resilience, and capacity across the infrastructure lifecycle.

Planning and Assessment

Self-direct development of business-impactful platforms and capabilities suitable for SVP/GE-level consumption.
Decision-maker for roadmap direction and capability definition; own outcomes from the ideation and assessment process.

Other

Define and validate standard engineering processes; drive consistency and coaching across IaC, compliance, and agentic AI practices.
Demonstrate knowledge and authority across >50% of infrastructure domains; own platform and service definitions.
Shape strategies, missions, and mandate of platform engineering within TI; align to TI and T&O agenda.